coverage:
The paper has about 13.7k lines of LaTeX in 11 section files. I read Section 1 (introduction and proof map) in full, and all of Section 2. In Section 2 I checked these steps by hand:
- the outer-measure selection of a scale k;
- the slope and intercept density caps from smoothing;
- the three initial inequalities g(1,0) >= sigma, g(0,0) <= 0 and g(r,u) <= r + 2 - 2u;
- the endpoint maximization giving r0 > 0, u0 < 4 and the C(1-R) cap, plus the angular cap;
- the crop density transform;
- the slope-volume bound |Sigma| <= K a J / q^3, using the monic cubic Jacobian, the affine P_w good times and the area formula;
- the conclusion h >= sigma/6;
- the normalization and lifting algebra: B' = B/a_r, the d_ww bounds, the density factor J/nu and the endpoint cap transfer.

In Section 4, the first 350 lines: the definitions of d_*, k(d) and ell; the composition lemma; k > 0; the proof that the relative profile is linear, including the lower-secant contradiction; the nested systems; narrowness additivity; and the excluded-improvements arithmetic.

In Section 3: the full proof of the two-color matching lemma (jet scales, entropy palette, switching experiment, endpoint Jacobian, target-volume exponent 1/m + (m+1)/2, increment summation to d >= 1), and the opening of the terminal-extension lemma (label count and pair-mass Jensen).

In Section 6: the seven-direction tensor kernel lemma and the approximate real conic lemma. I checked the algebra by hand: the conic through 5 points, the q·L, q^2 and {0} kernels, and the injectivity of the two-copy test.

In Section 9: the setup, the nested-angle estimate, and the final completion of the main theorem.

I did not line-check most of Sections 5–8, the rest of 6, 06a, or most of 9: the scalar tools, the isotropic degree restoration, retained-edge planar rigidity, the horizontal model, the critical-rate and bootstrap propositions, and the full-time localization. I also did not check Section 10 (consequences).
